ly on substations and transformers. It is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria.\n- Norvane Utilities plans 2027 capex up 12%, with the same focus.\n- Together they make up about 56% of the utility order book at VLTX holdings (Pellham 35%, Norvane 21%).\n- These are plans, not firm orders, and they depend on financing. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, and equity markets have been less receptive. Whether the plans can be funded is the question n3 is working on.\n- I have no figures for smaller utilities or for the timing of orders within 2027.\n\n**Data centres (n6.r1):**\n- The outlook expects grid connection requests to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than in 2026, because power availability limits new sites.\n- Connection requests are only a proxy for equipment demand. I found no direct data on data-centre orders for transformers or switchgear.\n- The outlook is a single source with no time series to cross-check it.\n\n**Confidence:** moderate on direction, lower on the pace of growth. The main risk to the utility side is financing, and the main risk to the data-centre side is the power-availability limit.","ttft_ms":4155,"type":"result","duration_ms":29392,"uuid":"c5a670aa-1925-4955-8f95-9eb1b146398d","ttft_stream_ms":3115,"time_to_request_ms":159,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":14,"system_prompt":9,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":26,"input_hooks":7,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":19,"init_frame_send":5,"engine_pickup":7,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":16,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":2,"tool_schema_build":11,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":16},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":43,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":65,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":188,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":113,